    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Peers are often first-responders to mental health crises for college students. Peers are also often insufficiently prepared to respond effectively in these situations. College campuses are more reactive than preventative in their approach to mental health care. However, college freshmen are undergoing a significant period of transition when it is most critical to have the skillset to manage their own and support other’s mental health. Undergraduate freshmen need to recognize symptoms of depression and suicidal ideation, feel comfortable responding to a peer in need, and prioritize a healthy mind.\r\n    Huddle is an online learning experience for undergraduates on college campuses. This is an immersive experience integrated with peer health educator or residential advisory programs in residential dorm settings for students to build skills through a 3-step approach: 1) informing students about the warning signs of depression and suicidal ideation, 2) identify cues to appropriately support a peer in need, and 3) effectively navigate a conversation with a peer as a medium of support. If students can practice these skills in a safe, low-consequence environment, then they should feel more prepared to transfer these skills to real life and, in turn, have greater control over their own mental health care.\r\n    I anticipate that students will see an evident increase in confidence and comfort in acting as first-responders to mental health problems by their peers after engaging with Huddle over a few weeks in their first-year in college. A high functioning prototype of Huddle has been tested with freshmen for success in learning and usability. This feedback will inform the design of Huddle as a fully functioning product.\r\n    Huddle cultivates supportive college communities by empowering college freshmen to navigate difficult conversations about mental health with their peers.",
